    {
      "id": "CORE-CFG-RELOAD-03",
      "title": "In the uberjar, a reloaded configuration does not reach the adapter: the old adapter keeps running (known defect)",
      "tier": "core",
      "priority": "P1",
      "intent": "The update renames the schedule to S2, moves it to a second file target (sink v2) and changes an adapter-level setting: the counter's Min becomes 1000. S2 records prove the new configuration is running; their counter values show whether the adapter got it too. SimulatorAdapter.newInstance creates its adapter only if the companion-object field is still null (SimulatorAdapter.kt:213-214; the field is declared at :239) and stop() does not clear it (:194-195). In the uberjar the class comes from the system class loader, so the field survives the reload: the schedule and target change, but the counter keeps counting from the first configuration and Min 1000 is silently ignored until a restart. The same companion-object pattern is in the ads, j1939, modbus-tcp, mqtt, nats, pccc, rest, s7 and slmp adapters. Uberjar only; in-process is correct (CORE-CFG-RELOAD-02).",
