    {
      "id": "CORE-CFG-RELOAD-04",
      "title": "In IPC mode, a reloaded configuration does not reach the adapter service: the old adapter keeps serving (known defect)",
      "tier": "core",
      "priority": "P1",
      "intent": "The update renames the schedule to S2, moves it to a second file target (sink v2) and changes an adapter-level setting: the counter's Min becomes 1000. S2 records prove the new configuration is running; their counter values show whether the adapter got it too. IpcAdapterService.initializeAdapter inverts its check: a configuration that differs from the last one is only recorded (IpcAdapterService.kt:217-218), and the adapter is (re)created only when the same configuration arrives a second time (:219-253). After the reload sfc-main initialises the service with the new configuration, the service just records it, and the reads keep coming from the adapter built from the first one, so Min 1000 never applies. The same inversion makes every IPC run's first read fail with UNKNOWN and succeed only on sfc-main's retry 10 s later, which re-sends the identical configuration. IPC only.",
